  "final_message": "I reverted the `channel` removal by hand, so `OrderPlaced` should now carry `channel` again and the ARCH-4 check should pass. I haven't run `npm test`, `npm run arch` or `npm run typecheck`, because the shell is still denied. Please re-run CI to confirm.\n\nThe earlier premise was wrong. `analytics-ingest` declares `OrderPlaced.channel` as a required enum (`web|store|marketplace`), so `channel` is not unused. That contract isn't in this repo, so I couldn't see it when I made the change.\n\nI restored `channel` to the order model, the event, request validation and parsing, the tests, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. Each file should now match its original, but I couldn't diff against git to prove it. `git diff` will show whether anything differs from the base commit.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. After that, the removal can be redone along with a `schemaVersion` bump to 4 for `OrderPlaced`. I can redo it when you say so.",
